    "background_story": "Collin was a brilliant and unorthodox dentist who had a fascination with the intricacies of the human mouth. He spent years studying the anatomy of the oral cavity, with a particular focus on the orifice of the mouth. His colleagues often joked that he knew more about the nuances of the lips, tongue, and teeth than anyone else in the field. Collin's expertise led to breakthroughs in dental surgery, allowing him to develop innovative procedures for repairing damaged orifices. His work improved the lives of countless patients, restoring their ability to eat, speak, and smile with confidence. Despite his intense focus on the oral orifice, Collin's patients adored him for his gentle bedside manner and kind smile.",
